<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main class="flex-grow py-12 sm:py-20">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <div class="border-b-2 border-tbf-navy pb-6 mb-8">
      <span class="tbf-category-badge text-xs">Governance & Ethics</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mt-2">
        Policies, Ethics & AI Disclosures
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-2">
        Last updated: August 2026 · The Bombay Forum Editorial Standards
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Tabbed Policy Content -->
    <div class="space-y-12 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-800 font-sans leading-relaxed">
      
      <!-- Section 1: Editorial Independence & AI Disclosures -->
      <section id="ai-ethics" class="pb-10 border-b border-tbf-border">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mb-4">
          1. Editorial Independence & AI Disclosures
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The Bombay Forum utilises computational intelligence and automated ingestion pipelines to survey thousands of global and domestic news feeds, financial data streams, and regulatory filings.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4 font-bold text-tbf-navy">
          Crucially, our operational architecture strictly adheres to a mandatory human editorial gate (Rule 5.2). No article, profile, or market dispatch is ever published autonomously without rigorous human review, fact verification, and substantive line-editing by a senior editor.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where external reportage serves as the basis for analysis, we provide transparent attribution and links to the original investigative work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Privacy Policy -->
      <section id="privacy" class="pb-10 border-b border-tbf-border">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mb-4">
          2. Privacy Policy
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          We respect the privacy of our readers and subscribers. We collect only necessary information:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li><strong>Newsletter Subscribers:</strong> Your email address is stored securely to deliver <em>The Saturday Communiqué</em>. We never sell, rent, or trade our subscriber database to third parties.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> We use privacy-preserving aggregate telemetry to monitor reading time and popular categories to inform our editorial coverage.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You may unsubscribe from our communications at any time via the one-click link included in every newsletter footer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Terms of Service -->
      <section id="terms" class="pb-10 border-b border-tbf-border">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mb-4">
          3. Terms of Service
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          All content published on The Bombay Forum—including text, layout designs, signature photography curations, and branding—is protected under Indian and international copyright laws.
        </p>
        <p>
          Material may not be reproduced, republished, or syndicated without prior written consent from the Editor-in-Chief. Fair use quotes with appropriate attribution and backlink to the original article are welcomed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Cookie Policy -->
      <section id="cookies">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mb-4">
          4. Cookie Policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          We use minimal first-party cookies necessary for session authentication (for editors) and to remember reading preferences. We do not deploy invasive third-party cross-site ad trackers.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

  </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
